    "statement": "At m=2 over F_97 there is an explicit T=rho+2 incidence pattern with exact one-deficit saturation, a canonical minimum pair union W of size 12, pair intersections at most two, and bad overlap 2>1. Its third-root datum is nu_x=x+x^(-1)=(x^2+1)/x, so the old bivariate matrix M_W has rank 11<12 with an all-nonzero kernel. The coefficient values do not extend to X-degree rho; the strengthened matrix C_W=[M_W;E_W] has rank 12. This fences incidence-only full rank and is not a Hankel or Prize counterexample.",
